            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Keloidal scarring can complicate surgical procedures.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">This 21-month-old African-American child developed a keloid around his tracheostomy that extended into the trachea.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Keloidal formation from a tracheostomy site can extend into the trachea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
